WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:04.820
These days, shows aren't exactly afraid to
kill off a main character or two — especially

00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:09.240
if it serves the story, or the show gets a
little extra social media attention in the

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:10.000
process.

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:16.760
Here is a spoiler filled look at some TV character
deaths on major shows in 2019 that were unthinkable…

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:18.360
but still totally happened.

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:22.700
Game of Thrones wrapped up a number of character
arcs in its eighth season the way Game of

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:25.920
Thrones likes to do: with a grisly on-screen
death.

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:30.740
The Battle of Winterfell was an event that
the series has long been building up to, and

00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:35.120
promised an absolute resolution to one of
the show's biggest storylines.

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:39.880
After all, how could the show's various groups
and families vie for the Iron Throne if they

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:43.980
couldn't fight off the Night King and the
massive undead army under his control?

00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:48.450
In the end, the army of the living seemed
helpless to stop it all, save for the lucky

00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:50.700
intervention of a certain assassin.

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:53.920
"What do we say to the God of Death?"

00:00:57.960 --> 00:00:58.960
"Not today."

00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:04.720
And so the Night King's reign was brought
to a swift end by Arya Stark and her Valyrian

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:09.080
steel dagger — instantly destroying every
last undead soldier in the process.

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:13.799
While Gotham serves as a prequel series to
the well-established events of the Batman

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:18.560
comics and movies, the show easily grew into
its own over the course of five seasons.

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:24.090
It also deviated a fair bit from its source
material, delivering the occasional surprise

00:01:24.090 --> 00:01:28.980
plot twist that didn't quite match up with
what Batman fans might have expected to happen.

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:34.340
A year ago, Tabitha felt the wrath of Oswald
Cobblepot, also known as the Penguin, in his

00:01:34.340 --> 00:01:37.160
convoluted revenge plot over the death of
his mother.

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:42.680
Butch, once dead and resurrected as the grotesque
Solomon Grundy, struck up a tender relationship

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:45.480
with Tabitha, who is otherwise known as Tigress.

00:01:45.609 --> 00:01:49.900
The Penguin killed Butch right in front of
Tabitha, adding injury to insult by shooting

00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:52.520
her in the leg, swearing to finish her off
someday.

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:58.200
She did manage to survive into Gotham's final
season… but only to fulfill Oswald's prophecy.

00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:04.499
At the height of 2019's "No Man's Land" plot
arc, Cobblepot finally stabs and kills poor

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:05.060
Tabitha.

00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:10.600
Based on Neil Gaiman's legendary novel, Showtime's
American Gods operates on the conceit that

00:02:10.610 --> 00:02:15.470
all the gods anyone has ever believed in are
real, and that they wander around the U.S.

00:02:15.470 --> 00:02:19.380
in human form, having been brought to the
new world hundreds of years prior.

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:25.220
And while you might assume that gods are pretty
much unkillable, American Gods doesn't agree.

00:02:25.220 --> 00:02:31.740
The show had no qualms, then, in bumping off
Mad Sweeney, an ancient Irish king-turned-bird-turned-six-foot-tall-leprechaun.

00:02:32.030 --> 00:02:36.260
In the present day, this scrappy god worked
as muscle for Mr. Wednesday, leader of the

00:02:36.260 --> 00:02:37.120
old gods.

00:02:37.330 --> 00:02:42.480
Early in the series, however, Mad Sweeney's
magical powers failed when he lost his enchanted

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:42.980
coin.

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:47.970
His luck and good fortune having come to an
end, Sweeney finds himself unable to understand

00:02:47.970 --> 00:02:49.580
why his life is falling apart.

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:55.091
Driven to madness, he turns on Shadow Moon,
the show's lead... only for Shadow to stab

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:55.780
him in the heart.

00:02:56.460 --> 00:03:01.140
Veep's series finale sees lead character Selina
Meyer become President of the United States

00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:05.460
after a series of machinations and manipulations
at her party's national convention.

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:10.200
Selina gets the nomination when she courts
Jonah Ryan's support by making him her running

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:14.380
mate, and gets Buddy Calhoun on board by agreeing
to ban same-sex marriage.

00:03:14.620 --> 00:03:19.360
One final roadblock is swiftly overcome after
Meyer frames her loyal assistant Gary for

00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:21.240
corruption and has him sent to prison.

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:28.400
"I couldn't have done it without you.  Don't worry I'm not going
anywhere."

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:34.960
The episode then flashes forward to Selina
in the Oval Office, and then to more than

00:03:34.960 --> 00:03:40.180
20 years later, when Selina's press secretary
turned CBS News reporter Mike McLintock covers

00:03:40.180 --> 00:03:41.720
the ex-president's funeral.

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:46.720
Veep saves one last joke for its put-upon
protagonist, when Mike interrupts and then

00:03:46.730 --> 00:03:50.870
ends his coverage of the presidential memorial
to pursue the breaking news that beloved actor

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:52.380
Tom Hanks has died.

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:57.200
It sometimes seemed like the story of Game
of Thrones was really the story of Daenerys

00:03:57.210 --> 00:04:01.960
Targaryen — Mother of Dragons, Khaleesi
of the Great Grass Sea, and heir to the Iron

00:04:01.960 --> 00:04:02.460
Throne.

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:07.420
Unfortunately, Dany's story came to a very
final end in the show's last episode.

00:04:07.820 --> 00:04:12.800
Worn down by her relentless quest for power
and the deaths of her allies, the show's final

00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:17.480
chapters saw her succumb to madness and burn
down King's Landing with dragonfire.

00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:22.060
This decision, which caused the deaths of
countless innocents, also led to the loss

00:04:22.060 --> 00:04:27.480
of support from her lover and nephew Jon Snow,
as well as her chief advisor Tyrion Lannister.

00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:35.560
"I freed my brother… and you slaughtered
a city."

00:04:35.980 --> 00:04:39.920
After all Daenerys went through in Game of
Thrones over the years, it seems almost cruel

00:04:39.920 --> 00:04:42.200
that she came so close to a happy ending.

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:45.400
But any chance of that ended with her descent
into tyranny.

00:04:45.620 --> 00:04:49.880
To prevent Daenerys from inflicting her madness
on the rest of the world, Jon Snow stabbed

00:04:49.880 --> 00:04:52.900
her to death only feet from the throne she'd
always wanted.

00:04:53.380 --> 00:04:58.139
Supergirl killing off Lex Luthor is shocking
largely because he's by far the most famous

00:04:58.139 --> 00:05:02.830
rogue in the Superman mythos — and one of
the most notorious villains in superhero fiction

00:05:02.830 --> 00:05:03.480
altogether.

00:05:03.560 --> 00:05:06.540
With his death, where does Supergirl even
go from there?

00:05:06.820 --> 00:05:11.940
Well, in his final moments of life Lex reveals
that Kara Danvers and Supergirl are one and

00:05:11.940 --> 00:05:12.620
the same.

00:05:12.940 --> 00:05:17.390
It was a tantalizing cliffhanger, as well
as an inglorious end to a season-long arc

00:05:17.390 --> 00:05:20.580
for the evil industrialist, politician, and
super-villain.

00:05:20.860 --> 00:05:24.540
After all, all he ever really wanted to do
was defeat Superman.

00:05:24.820 --> 00:05:26.040
And kill Lois Lane.

00:05:26.540 --> 00:05:28.640
And create an evil Supergirl clone.

00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:30.640
Is that really so bad?

